Body:
**tl;dr** This is already resolved on v1.2.11.

## Explanation

The root cause was in `@opentui/core`, in the `extractCompleteSequences()` function in `stdin-buffer.ts`. When typed text arrives (not pasted — paste uses a separate code path), the `stdin` buffer splits the input into individual character sequences using `remaining[0]` / `pos++`. These operate on UTF-16 code units, not Unicode codepoints. Characters above `U+FFFF` (emojis, some CJK, etc.) are stored in JS as surrogate pairs — two code units — and the old code splits them into two lone surrogates, each of which becomes `U+FFFD` downstream.

Fixed in: OpenTUI 0.1.80 via:
- https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui/pull/682

First OpenCode release with the fix: v1.2.11 (upgrades to opentui 0.1.81)

## Patch

For anyone still on OpenCode 1.1.47 (opentui 0.1.75), here's a minimal patch against the compiled JS in `node_modules` (works on NixOS). The fix checks whether a UTF-16 code unit is a high surrogate followed by a low surrogate, and if so keeps both together as a single sequence entry:

```diff
--- packages/opencode/node_modules/@opentui/core/index-s0q9547t.js.orig
+++ packages/opencode/node_modules/@opentui/core/index-s0q9547t.js
@@ -6055,8 +6055,23 @@
         return { sequences, remainder: remaining };
       }
     } else {
-      sequences.push(remaining[0]);
-      pos++;
+      const code = remaining.charCodeAt(0);
+      if (code >= 0xd800 && code <= 0xdbff) {
+        if (remaining.length === 1) {
+          return { sequences, remainder: remaining };
+        }
+        const next = remaining.charCodeAt(1);
+        if (next >= 0xdc00 && next <= 0xdfff) {
+          sequences.push(remaining.slice(0, 2));
+          pos += 2;
+        } else {
+          sequences.push(remaining[0]);
+          pos++;
+        }
+      } else {
+        sequences.push(remaining[0]);
+        pos++;
+      }
     }
   }
   return { sequences, remainder: "" };
```

For **Anthropic direct API** users, I made a plugin that injects the `context-1m-2025-08-07` beta header via `chat.headers` hook — it appends to existing SDK beta flags (claude-code, interleaved-thinking, etc.) instead of replacing them.

Add to your `opencode.json`:
```jsonc
{
  "plugin": ["opencode-anthropic-context-1m"],
  "provider": {
    "anthropic": {
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4-6":          { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 128000 } },
        "claude-sonnet-4-6":        { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 64000 } },
        "claude-sonnet-4-5":        { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 64000 } },
        "claude-sonnet-4-20250514": { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 64000 } }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `plugin` entry injects the beta header. The `provider.anthropic.models` entries override the default 200K limit so auto-compaction triggers at ~968K instead of ~168K.

