The premature compaction at ~200k is caused by two things: (1) missing `context-1m-2025-08-07` beta header, and (2) default model limits in OpenCode being set to 200k.

For **Anthropic API** users, I made a plugin that fixes both. Add to your `opencode.json`:

```jsonc
{
  "plugin": ["opencode-anthropic-context-1m"],
  "provider": {
    "anthropic": {
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4-6":          { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 128000 } },
        "claude-sonnet-4-6":        { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 64000 } },
        "claude-sonnet-4-5":        { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 64000 } },
        "claude-sonnet-4-20250514": { "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 64000 } }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The plugin injects the beta header via `chat.headers` hook (appends, doesn't overwrite existing SDK flags). The model overrides push compaction threshold from ~168K to ~968K.

https://github.com/DusKing1/opencode-anthropic-context-1m

The plugin at https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/12338#issuecomment-3909808717 didn't work for me. But I found a much simpler approach to set the header in the OpenCode config:

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "anthropic": {
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4-6": {
          "limit": {
            "context": 1000000,
            "output": 128000
          },
          "headers": {
            "anthropic-beta": "context-1m-2025-08-07"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

I didn't find any documentation but I looked at the JSON schema for the OpenCode config and found the `headers` key there: https://opencode.ai/config.json.
